WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
What should we call this class? Hilchot Mamrim? Chapter 1? Chapter 1. Okay.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:15.000
It is, in effect, it is a continuation of our class on Naran.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Let me explain to you what I want to do here and the value.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.000
In the last class, we read critically once a month.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
That's what we did.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:42.000
And what we tried to show is that you cannot read a paragraph in the Shoharuch as you read, you know, a book in history.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:50.000
That every word is a code for something that either you studied independently or you did not.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:02.000
And that the average reader, unless he happens to be a scholar, cannot understand what the Shoharuch is saying.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
I mean, it seems easy.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
I called Naran the master of ambiguity.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Every term, if you pay attention, it is an ambiguous term.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
And that his popularity is because he was ambiguous.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Now, here today we're going to study something extraordinary about rabbinic authority.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.000
And I'm going to anticipate.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Basically, what Harambam is going to say, that the rabbinic authority today is terribly limited.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:46.000
We have to, you know, and now comes one expression that you heard a thousand times.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
And the connection between this chapter and Naran.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Kibalnu alenu hora'at Naran.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Which means, it's not that he is the supreme authority, but we, kibalnu alenu hora'at Naran.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Other people didn't do it, no problem.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.000
But this is our standard.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.000
That's more or less the purpose of the...

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.000
It's not that we claim that everybody has to submit themselves to the sake of Naran, no.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.000
There's other communities we respect and we love and so on.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
But, so what is the basis?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Kibalnu alenu hora'at Naran.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
That's what I wanted to say.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:41.000
Now, before I proceed, I guess that you may have some...

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Go ahead, ask me questions, I'll present a bunch of you and so on.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.000
The communities...

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.000
I wrote a whole article about it.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Is there any historical records that say...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.000
No.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.000
There isn't such a thing.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
I'm sure there is no record to this.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000
But that is what we say.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.000
And because we say so, it is so because we say so.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.000
It's a very popular...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.000
It's a popular... and so on.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.000
One thing is, you showed last week that Naran has a lot of...

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.000
Kibalnu alenu hora'at Naran.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.000
So there's a lot of flexibility.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
And also, which is true, yes?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
That is a frame of reference.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.000
You could go against them in a polite way, yes?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.000
You could go this.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.000
So it is a frame of reference.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000
It's not a code, the traffic code of New York State.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.000
No, it's not the same thing, yes?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.000
And therefore, the...

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.000
But that's why I believe that you cannot have a function, a function...

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.000
without a...

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.000
I mean, otherwise, you know, it's very...

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.000
You need a competent hacham, like we used to have, a competent hachamim,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:16.000
and to be able to navigate and to, you know, about what...

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000
How about, Aaron, do you read for us?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.000
Yes?

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.000
So I think we say something.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.000
Harambam is unique, yes?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.000
We don't have to say it.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.000
And one of the nice things that it does,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.000
to take this, you know,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.000
is to...

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.000
to give you the mesvot min ha-Torah,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.000
the pesokim min ha-Torah.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.000
It's very nice to say,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.000
what is the source?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.000
What is the source?

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
We are people of the law, yes?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.000
What is the source?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.000
So you're going to be saved.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.000
No, no, no.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.000
No, no.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.000
This has to do...

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
You have to remember.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.000
We have three sources of authority,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.000
and each one is independent of the other.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Alright?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.000
One of them is the Supreme Court.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.000
And no keter can tell the other what to do.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.000
The separation between church and state of America is taken from us.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Yes?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Keter Torah and Keter Markud.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.000
The whole independence of the Supreme Court is taken from us.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Yes?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.000
So we serve...

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.000
I mean, I have in a book,

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.000
The Horizontal Society,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.000
in the last section I show

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.000
that the pilgrims,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.000
when they came to America,

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.000
they took our Torah, the Tanakh,

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
not the new thing that they have,

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.000
as a model

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.000
for what was, or what is,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.000
the most successful democracy in the world.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Yes?

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.000
And so I just wanted you to know

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.000
that the basis of modern democracy

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.000
is not Greeks.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.000
Yes?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.000
It's the Torah.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.000
Alright?

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.000
If you want to know about tyranny,

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.000
and all those despots and so on,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.000
all those are Greek words.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Yes?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Alright?

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.000
So the first one is

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.000
la'asot al piya torah

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.000
shambulano bedina gadol.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.000
It's not the Torah in abstract.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.000
I'm going to use a word

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.000
and I don't mean it in an irresponsible way.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.000
The Torah shevichtav

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.000
is like the edab in Arabic,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.000
the education.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
That is our values.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.000
Yes?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.000
The law,

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.000
which is implemented,

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.000
and is enforced,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.000
is not by reading the Torah.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.000
It's our education.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.000
It's by the Supreme Court.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.000
In this way was also modeled the Constitution.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.000
You could read the Constitution

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.000
as a piece of political philosophy, etc.,

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.000
but whatever interpretation you give

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.000
is meaningless

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.000
unless it was expressed

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.000
by the Supreme Court of America.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.000
So therefore you could read

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.000
the Constitution as, I don't know,

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.000
the history of the human interest.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Whatever it is, fine.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.000
But that is not binding.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.000
Binding is what the Supreme Court says.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.000
Alright?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.000
And the same thing is with us.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.000
What the bedina gadol says,

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.000
that is.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.000
I'll give you an example.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.000
There could be a trillion professors and scholars

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.000
and they say,

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.000
and tell me what the word

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.000
utotafot ben yarecha means.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.000
But this has absolutely no bearing

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.000
on my putting tefillin.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.000
I put tefillin the way it is

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.000
because the Supreme Court of Israel,

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.000
bedina gadol,

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.000
said that it is so.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.000
Alright?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.000
So when people question

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.000
the right of the bedina gadol,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.000
I would like also to question

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:06.000
the right of the Supreme Court of America.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.000
They will not dare do that.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Alright? Fine.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.000
Very good.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
So we have bedina gadol,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.000
which I always refer to bedina gadol,

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.000
I refer to it as

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.000
the Supreme Court of Israel.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Alright?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Our scholars say differently,

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.000
no problem.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.000
You as a scholar,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.000
you can say anything you want

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.000
about the Constitution of America.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.000
But it's not binding.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.000
And the judges sitting at the Supreme Court

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.000
do not even have to relate to it.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.000
Alright?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.000
Clear?

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.000
Fine?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.000
All the critical criticism,

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.000
this and that,

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.000
it's, you know,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.000
it's not binding.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Chavot.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.000
Yes?

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.000
It's a misal haseh

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:58.000
to do al piah torah shey yorucha.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.000
And also,

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.000
lo tasul menadabra shey yorucha

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.000
yamil usmol.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.000
What happens if I don't do it?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.000
Over a lot of haseh.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.000
Fine.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Chavot.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.000
One second,

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.000
I'll be with you.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.000
Yes?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.000
Nobody,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.000
in that they say,

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.000
huh,

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.000
I know that sometimes in the,

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.000
we want to preach to the people and so on,

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.000
and we say,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.000
the Torah says this.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.000
No.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.000
I mean,

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.000
you could say,

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.000
you should use a different kind of word.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.000
You have to say what the Torah says

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.000
is what the Torah says.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.000
What we imagine the Torah should say here,

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.000
we say,

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
this is a different way to say it.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.000
But don't,

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.000
don't,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.000
don't,

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.000
lo tosiva ra Torah.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.000
You see?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.000
And,

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.000
and now one way,

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.000
again now,

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.000
hachamim,

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.000
we're very careful.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.000
Not everything that I imagine

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.000
the kahal should do,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.000
yes,

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.000
is in the Torah.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.000
Yes?

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.000
And you say,

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.000
well,

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.000
no,

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.000
but the pirush of this,

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.000
listen,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.000
the pirush was given to us,

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.000
baruch Hashem,

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.000
by Beit Din HaKadon,

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.000
because this is in the Talmud,

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.000
so I'm fine.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
And you could,

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.000
and you could say that we should do that,

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.000
and no,

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.000
no problem.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.000
But don't tell me that this is in the Torah.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.000
You know?

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.000
All right?

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.000
So,

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.000
so for us,

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.000
the Torah is something very,

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.000
very holy,

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.000
very,

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.000
very sacred.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.000
We don't play with it.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.000
And,

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.000
and,

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.000
and that's why serecha,

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.000
I'm not preaching.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.000
I'm trying to say that's why,

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.000
that's why we didn't have anti-Torah movements

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.000
among us,

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.000
baruch Hashem,

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.000
because we didn't put everything with it.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.000
The,

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.000
the preacher at that time was,

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.000
was,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.000
you know,

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.000
and so on,

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.000
and he was right,

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.000
the preacher.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.000
But he said,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.000
this is the Torah,

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.000
this is the Torah,

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.000
and then people said,

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.000
well,

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.000
this is the Torah,

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.000
I mean,

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.000
this is how it's going to be.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.000
The Torah is something from Borei HaOlam,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.000
yes,

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.000
something that,

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.000
that we cannot imitate.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.000
Really,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.000
we cannot imitate it.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.000
Just like you,

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.000
and so on.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.000
I think that you are,

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.000
yes.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.000
So,

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.000
so this is really the,

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.000
the banan

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.000
from the Beidim HaGadol

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.000
are really

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.000
Yeah.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.000
I mean,

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.000
No,

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.000
no,

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.000
no,

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.000
no,

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.000
no,

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.000
no.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.000
I'm going to give you an example.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.000
The,

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.000
this,

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.000
Lechem Mishneh says further,

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.000
I mean,

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.000
we don't have,

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.000
we've been to all of it.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.000
If I,

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.000
you ask me,

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.000
what do I have to make

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.000
Mekinat HaZayim?

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.000
I have to tell you,

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.000
this is,

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.000
yes,

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.000
it's the Rabbanan.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.000
And I could give you,

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.000
try to,

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.000
to,

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.000
you know,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.000
impress upon you

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.000
why you should do it.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.000
