How?

00:58:20.120 --> 00:58:23.120
Because the Torah authorized the B'ten to do it.

00:58:24.120 --> 00:58:29.120
And therefore, if you are disrespectful,

00:58:29.120 --> 00:58:31.120
you are disrespecting God.

00:58:31.120 --> 00:58:34.120
God gave him the authority to do that.

00:58:34.120 --> 00:58:39.120
You say, don't do it, or do it, or this.

00:58:39.120 --> 00:58:45.120
But don't be disrespectful because you are questioning God

00:58:45.120 --> 00:58:51.120
who gave them the authority to promulgate Nusa Yagin.

00:58:51.120 --> 00:58:52.120
Submit an argument?

00:58:52.120 --> 00:58:53.120
Yeah, no.

00:58:53.120 --> 00:58:57.120
The point is you could always holek.

00:58:57.120 --> 00:59:00.120
And the question is that he's moreh.

00:59:00.120 --> 00:59:01.120
Right.

00:59:01.120 --> 00:59:08.120
I mean, not only holek, but even maran,

00:59:08.120 --> 00:59:11.120
which is for us the supreme authority.

00:59:11.120 --> 00:59:14.120
Many times, without saying that we holkeem,

00:59:14.120 --> 00:59:16.120
the posek is holek.

00:59:17.120 --> 00:59:24.120
You do it with the recheres.

00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:28.120
Yes, never questioning the authority.

00:59:28.120 --> 00:59:33.120
Because the truth is, that's one of the great Hiddush I have,

00:59:33.120 --> 00:59:38.120
that you could be a fantastic posek without being disrespectful.

00:59:38.120 --> 00:59:42.120
You don't have to disrespect anybody.

00:59:42.120 --> 00:59:44.120
You're not doing fine.

00:59:44.120 --> 00:59:48.120
There's a nice way how to say it about the ziz,

00:59:48.120 --> 00:59:50.120
and Aharon said to him, you smoke a ziz,

00:59:50.120 --> 00:59:56.120
because there's a whole rhetoric, there's an art of being polite.

00:59:56.120 --> 00:59:58.120
And you'll be polite.

00:59:58.120 --> 01:00:03.120
That's why I believe that the mambrim, also with your father and mother,

01:00:03.120 --> 01:00:10.120
now you're married, you have children, but your father asked you this.

01:00:10.120 --> 01:00:11.120
How are you going to say no?

01:00:11.120 --> 01:00:13.120
That's very important.

01:00:13.120 --> 01:00:14.120
Don't offend them.

01:00:14.120 --> 01:00:15.120
Don't do it.

01:00:15.120 --> 01:00:16.120
Don't do it.

01:00:16.120 --> 01:00:17.120
That's what I'm saying.

01:00:17.120 --> 01:00:21.120
I like very much that the rabbi just supposed,

01:00:21.120 --> 01:00:24.120
the beddina gadon, and shirem ze genim,

01:00:24.120 --> 01:00:27.120
and there's ways to do it, and so on.

01:00:27.120 --> 01:00:29.120
Don't be disrespectful.

01:00:29.120 --> 01:00:31.120
You're not fine.

01:00:31.120 --> 01:00:32.120
Don't be disrespectful.

01:00:32.120 --> 01:00:33.120
Chavot.

01:00:36.120 --> 01:00:39.120
Even the minhak, established by the beddin, for instance,

01:00:39.120 --> 01:00:42.120
shenei yamim tovim.

01:00:42.120 --> 01:00:50.120
Actually, it's in other studies, because it's not universal.

01:00:50.120 --> 01:00:52.120
This is minhak torah.

01:00:52.120 --> 01:00:53.120
Why is minhak torah?

01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:55.120
Ah, it's not written two days in the torah.

01:00:55.120 --> 01:00:58.120
Because the authority to do it is minhak torah.

01:00:58.120 --> 01:00:59.120
Now, there is a typical question.

01:00:59.120 --> 01:01:06.120
Everybody asks a question, and I think the question is not based upon logic.

01:01:06.120 --> 01:01:08.120
The Ramban is the first one.

01:01:09.120 --> 01:01:10.120
Then, the hachamim says,

01:01:14.120 --> 01:01:17.120
If the Ramban is also the authority,

01:01:17.120 --> 01:01:19.120
so everything should be minhak torah.

01:01:19.120 --> 01:01:20.120
Do you understand the question?

01:01:22.120 --> 01:01:25.120
So, in my book, Yirim Be'er Sheva Rambam,

01:01:25.120 --> 01:01:27.120
I point out,

01:01:27.120 --> 01:01:28.120
that according to Ramban,

01:01:28.120 --> 01:01:32.120
minhak torah is minhak torah for everyone.

01:01:32.120 --> 01:01:37.120
This that says minhak torah is minhak torah for the hachamim.

01:01:37.120 --> 01:01:39.120
So, therefore, heim amru.

01:01:39.120 --> 01:01:40.120
Heim amru.

01:01:40.120 --> 01:01:42.120
The question is not a question.

01:01:42.120 --> 01:01:43.120
All right?

01:01:43.120 --> 01:01:45.120
Could you explain?

01:01:45.120 --> 01:01:50.120
If all those non-de'oraita laws, de'oraita?

01:01:50.120 --> 01:01:52.120
Would you have a safik?

01:01:52.120 --> 01:01:56.120
Safik to Rabbanan also le'humla.

01:01:56.120 --> 01:01:58.120
Because Rabbanan gets the authority from minhak torah.

01:01:58.120 --> 01:01:59.120
Yeah, yeah.

01:01:59.120 --> 01:02:00.120
So, how come the hachamim says,

01:02:00.120 --> 01:02:02.120
Safik to Rabbanan ded le'kulla?

01:02:02.120 --> 01:02:04.120
So, I answer.

01:02:05.120 --> 01:02:07.120
According to Ramban,

01:02:07.120 --> 01:02:11.120
every safik is le'kulla.

01:02:11.120 --> 01:02:14.120
It says safik de'oraita le'humla.

01:02:14.120 --> 01:02:16.120
This, that we make safik de'oraita le'humla,

01:02:16.120 --> 01:02:18.120
is the Rabbanan.

01:02:18.120 --> 01:02:21.120
The rabbi is saying that safik de'oraita le'humla,

01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:24.120
and the rabbi is saying safik de'oraita le'kulla.

01:02:24.120 --> 01:02:25.120
Do you understand?

01:02:25.120 --> 01:02:28.120
The Torah doesn't say safik le'humla.

01:02:28.120 --> 01:02:30.120
Do you understand?

01:02:30.120 --> 01:02:31.120
Sure.

01:02:32.120 --> 01:02:34.120
Safik de'oraita?

01:02:34.120 --> 01:02:35.120
We don't know what to do.

01:02:35.120 --> 01:02:36.120
No.

01:02:36.120 --> 01:02:40.120
Safik de'oraita is actually minhak torah le'kulla,

01:02:40.120 --> 01:02:41.120
because the Torah doesn't...

01:02:41.120 --> 01:02:43.120
See, I tell you why.

01:02:43.120 --> 01:02:44.120
You don't understand.

01:02:44.120 --> 01:02:46.120
Because the Torah is a positive system.

01:02:46.120 --> 01:02:48.120
Whatever the Torah doesn't say,

01:02:48.120 --> 01:02:50.120
is mutar.

01:02:50.120 --> 01:02:52.120
All right?

01:02:52.120 --> 01:02:54.120
So now, there's no place the Torah says,

01:02:54.120 --> 01:02:58.120
Safik de'oraita le'humla.

01:02:58.120 --> 01:02:59.120
So, no place.

01:02:59.120 --> 01:03:00.120
So therefore...

01:03:00.120 --> 01:03:02.120
Ah, but...

01:03:02.120 --> 01:03:04.120
Gemara all over, safik de'oraita le'humla,

01:03:04.120 --> 01:03:07.120
Hakamim say that's safik de'oraita le'humla.

01:03:07.120 --> 01:03:09.120
And therefore, the Hakamim could say,

01:03:09.120 --> 01:03:12.120
safik de'oraita le'kulla,

01:03:12.120 --> 01:03:15.120
that's a positive system.

01:03:17.120 --> 01:03:19.120
Also, there's many proofs for it.

01:03:19.120 --> 01:03:21.120
Humre shiteyamim.

01:03:21.120 --> 01:03:23.120
Now, matillim, that's the Torah?

01:03:23.120 --> 01:03:25.120
That's the Rabbanan.

01:03:25.120 --> 01:03:28.120
I mean, how could you be more explicit than that?

01:03:29.120 --> 01:03:31.120
But the simple thing is,

01:03:31.120 --> 01:03:33.120
the Torah is a positive system.

01:03:33.120 --> 01:03:36.120
Whatever is not forbidden in the Torah,

01:03:36.120 --> 01:03:38.120
is permitted.

01:03:40.120 --> 01:03:42.120
Positive system.

01:03:43.120 --> 01:03:45.120
Positive legal system.

01:03:48.120 --> 01:03:50.120
Yeah, go ahead.

01:03:50.120 --> 01:03:52.120
Right.

01:03:53.120 --> 01:03:55.120
Read it, read it.

01:03:58.120 --> 01:04:00.120
Ah, shelo b'zma'a tz'alavim.

01:04:02.120 --> 01:04:04.120
Shelo b'zma'a tz'alavim.

01:04:04.120 --> 01:04:06.120
Yes.

01:04:07.120 --> 01:04:09.120
Like now.

01:04:09.120 --> 01:04:11.120
Today.

01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:25.120
No, no, but you have a new case.

01:04:26.120 --> 01:04:28.120
A new case.

01:04:28.120 --> 01:04:30.120
By the way, that's one of the good things of the Torah.

01:04:30.120 --> 01:04:32.120
The Torah is constantly growing,

01:04:32.120 --> 01:04:34.120
because we always have new cases,

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:36.120
that we didn't have yesterday.

01:04:36.120 --> 01:04:39.120
And now, we have a Tuvet Din,

01:04:39.120 --> 01:04:41.120
not only is post,

01:04:41.120 --> 01:04:43.120
what's his name,

01:04:43.120 --> 01:04:46.120
is post Sanhedrin,

01:04:48.120 --> 01:04:51.120
maybe even post Talmud.

01:04:51.120 --> 01:04:53.120
We have two Tuvet Din in him.

01:04:53.120 --> 01:04:55.120
Two Tuvet Din.

01:04:55.120 --> 01:04:57.120
Yes.

01:04:59.120 --> 01:05:01.120
Yeah, but the whole point is,

01:05:01.120 --> 01:05:03.120
if you believe to one of the communities,

01:05:03.120 --> 01:05:05.120
I'm Ashkenazi, I'm Sephardi,

01:05:05.120 --> 01:05:07.120
I follow the community.

01:05:07.120 --> 01:05:09.120
But what happens if talking,

01:05:09.120 --> 01:05:11.120
that's why he speaks to you in singular,

01:05:11.120 --> 01:05:13.120
to a singular individual.

01:05:13.120 --> 01:05:15.120
Yes? All right?

01:05:15.120 --> 01:05:17.120
And I don't know.

01:05:17.120 --> 01:05:19.120
I don't belong to the Ashkenazi community,

01:05:19.120 --> 01:05:21.120
I don't belong to the Sephardi community.

01:05:22.120 --> 01:05:24.120
That's what Haram B'Av is speaking about.

01:05:24.120 --> 01:05:26.120
All right?

01:05:26.120 --> 01:05:28.120
It's also nice to have Ben B'Zehr.

01:05:28.120 --> 01:05:29.120
Yes.

01:05:29.120 --> 01:05:30.120
I hear today all the time,

01:05:30.120 --> 01:05:31.120
I turn them on.

01:05:31.120 --> 01:05:32.120
Nowadays, everybody says,

01:05:32.120 --> 01:05:33.120
we don't do that anymore.

01:05:33.120 --> 01:05:34.120
And I always say,

01:05:34.120 --> 01:05:36.120
well, why don't you?

01:05:36.120 --> 01:05:37.120
The Pharaoh Haram Ben Shimon is wrong?

01:05:37.120 --> 01:05:39.120
No, but we just don't do it anymore.

01:05:39.120 --> 01:05:41.120
Haram B'Av is saying here,

01:05:41.120 --> 01:05:43.120
the fact that you're in the time of Shidi Safeh,

01:05:43.120 --> 01:05:46.120
doesn't erase what the Pharaoh Haram Ben Shimon

01:05:46.120 --> 01:05:48.120
algorithm here.

01:05:48.120 --> 01:05:50.120
You don't have,

01:05:50.120 --> 01:05:52.120
you don't need it.

01:05:52.120 --> 01:05:53.120
But the most important thing here,

01:05:53.120 --> 01:05:54.120
I hate talking about somebody

01:05:54.120 --> 01:05:57.120
who does not belong to a community.

01:05:57.120 --> 01:05:58.120
If I belong to a community,

01:05:58.120 --> 01:06:00.120
I do what the community says.

01:06:00.120 --> 01:06:01.120
Don't like it? No problem.

01:06:01.120 --> 01:06:03.120
Move to another community.

01:06:03.120 --> 01:06:05.120
That's my position, yes?

01:06:05.120 --> 01:06:07.120
But you cannot be in one community

01:06:07.120 --> 01:06:11.120
and then disrupt the authority of that community.

01:06:11.120 --> 01:06:13.120
That's my position, yes?

01:06:13.120 --> 01:06:15.120
Don't like it?

01:06:16.120 --> 01:06:17.120
Big wolf.

01:06:17.120 --> 01:06:18.120
Yes?

01:06:18.120 --> 01:06:20.120
Now, what happens in case there's two Bedin,

01:06:20.120 --> 01:06:21.120
and I'm not a Tamei HaKam,

01:06:21.120 --> 01:06:24.120
I'm not a Tamei HaKam.

01:06:24.120 --> 01:06:26.120
What should I do?

01:06:26.120 --> 01:06:27.120
Yes?

01:06:29.120 --> 01:06:31.120
So there I tell you to follow the Chumra.

01:06:31.120 --> 01:06:32.120
In the Rabbanan,

01:06:32.120 --> 01:06:33.120
you follow the Kula,

01:06:33.120 --> 01:06:35.120
or if somebody is Gadol Mimen,

01:06:35.120 --> 01:06:36.120
you follow this.

01:06:36.120 --> 01:06:37.120
All right?

01:06:38.120 --> 01:06:40.120
We shall wait until 7 o'clock?

01:06:40.120 --> 01:06:42.120
Yes, we wait until 7 o'clock.

01:06:42.120 --> 01:06:43.120
Very good.

01:06:44.120 --> 01:06:46.120
Bar Mitzvah?

01:06:46.120 --> 01:06:47.120
Bar Mitzvah.

01:06:47.120 --> 01:06:48.120
All right.

01:06:49.120 --> 01:06:50.120
All right.

01:06:51.120 --> 01:06:53.120
Let's read the Halakha Giman.

01:06:53.120 --> 01:06:54.120
Okay.

01:06:54.120 --> 01:06:55.120
Yes.

01:06:55.120 --> 01:06:58.120
This is a decision for the world.

01:06:58.120 --> 01:06:59.120
For the world.

01:06:59.120 --> 01:07:02.120
If this is a decision on the law,

01:07:02.120 --> 01:07:04.120
you can be sure that this is not

01:07:04.120 --> 01:07:06.120
a decision from Moshe Messinai.

01:07:07.120 --> 01:07:08.120
Again.

01:07:09.120 --> 01:07:12.120
If this is a decision on the Talmud,

01:07:13.120 --> 01:07:14.120
or Mishnayot.

01:07:14.120 --> 01:07:15.120
Or Mishnayot.

01:07:16.120 --> 01:07:18.120
Or Rishonim, Aharonim.

01:07:19.120 --> 01:07:21.120
No, Rishonim, Aharonim, no, no, no, no.

01:07:21.120 --> 01:07:22.120
No.

01:07:22.120 --> 01:07:23.120
The Halakha is the Talmud.

01:07:23.120 --> 01:07:24.120
Then it cannot be,

01:07:24.120 --> 01:07:26.120
because whatever is Halakha,

01:07:26.120 --> 01:07:28.120
whatever we received from Moshe Rabbeinu

01:07:28.120 --> 01:07:32.120
is the absolute truth.

01:07:32.120 --> 01:07:34.120
I don't like using that term.

01:07:34.120 --> 01:07:35.120
All right?

01:07:35.120 --> 01:07:37.120
But this is absolute.

01:07:37.120 --> 01:07:39.120
This cannot be, you know,

01:07:39.120 --> 01:07:41.120
but I'm going to explain you why.

01:07:42.120 --> 01:07:44.120
I'm not going to use theology.

01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:46.120
I think you could re-characterize it.

01:07:46.120 --> 01:07:47.120
That's correct.

01:07:47.120 --> 01:07:48.120
And there's...

01:07:48.120 --> 01:07:49.120
You have presumptions...

01:07:49.120 --> 01:07:51.120
Let me say something very nice

01:07:51.120 --> 01:07:54.120
that I learned from Rabi Abraham,

01:07:54.120 --> 01:07:56.120
from the son of Arambam.

01:07:57.120 --> 01:07:59.120
A regular prophet,

01:07:59.120 --> 01:08:01.120
is a prophet,

01:08:01.120 --> 01:08:03.120
not because he receives the things

01:08:03.120 --> 01:08:05.120
directly from Bura Alam,

01:08:05.120 --> 01:08:08.120
but because Amal Akhtar himself.

01:08:09.120 --> 01:08:12.120
There's only one prophet

01:08:12.120 --> 01:08:14.120
that doesn't receive from Amal Akhtar

01:08:14.120 --> 01:08:15.120
but directly,

01:08:15.120 --> 01:08:17.120
Peh El Peh Eta Be Bo.

01:08:17.120 --> 01:08:19.120
And that's Moshe Rabbeinu.

01:08:19.120 --> 01:08:21.120
All right?

01:08:21.120 --> 01:08:23.120
So in a sense,

01:08:23.120 --> 01:08:24.120
in a very meticulous sense,

01:08:24.120 --> 01:08:26.120
Moshe Rabbeinu

01:08:26.120 --> 01:08:28.120
is Amal Akhtar Hashem.

01:08:28.120 --> 01:08:30.120
He's Shelech Hashem.

01:08:30.120 --> 01:08:32.120
So whatever...

01:08:32.120 --> 01:08:33.120
Just like a prophet,

01:08:33.120 --> 01:08:35.120
when he sees Amal Akhtar,

01:08:35.120 --> 01:08:36.120
he tells him something.

01:08:36.120 --> 01:08:38.120
The prophet, it has

01:08:38.120 --> 01:08:41.120
no ambiguity whatsoever.

01:08:41.120 --> 01:08:44.120
Whatever we listen from Moshe Rabbeinu,

01:08:44.120 --> 01:08:47.120
it's just that makes us prophets.

01:08:47.120 --> 01:08:50.120
Because we heard it from Amal Akhtar.

01:08:50.120 --> 01:08:52.120
Oh, you only heard it from Amal Akhtar.

01:08:52.120 --> 01:08:54.120
But every prophet

01:08:54.120 --> 01:08:56.120
only heard it from Amal Akhtar.

01:08:56.120 --> 01:08:58.120
So we are...

01:08:58.120 --> 01:08:59.120
You understand?

01:08:59.120 --> 01:09:02.120
Whatever we heard from Moshe Rabbeinu,

01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:04.120
we are in the same status

01:09:04.120 --> 01:09:06.120
as a prophet.

01:09:06.120 --> 01:09:08.120
Is this point clear?

01:09:08.120 --> 01:09:10.120
No ambiguities also.

01:09:10.120 --> 01:09:12.120
It definitely can't be no ambiguities.

01:09:12.120 --> 01:09:14.120
And there can't be no mahlukat.

01:09:14.120 --> 01:09:16.120
There's no certainty

01:09:16.120 --> 01:09:18.120
or certitude

01:09:18.120 --> 01:09:20.120
higher than that.

01:09:20.120 --> 01:09:22.120
Do you understand?

01:09:22.120 --> 01:09:24.120
So again,

01:09:24.120 --> 01:09:26.120
Yermiyah,

01:09:26.120 --> 01:09:28.120
who told Yermiyah whatever he told?

01:09:28.120 --> 01:09:30.120
Amal Akhtar,

01:09:30.120 --> 01:09:32.120
who spoke in the name of God.

01:09:32.120 --> 01:09:34.120
When by Yom B'taber

01:09:34.120 --> 01:09:36.120
Avonai and Moshe Lemor,

01:09:36.120 --> 01:09:38.120
and I hear it from Moshe Rabbeinu,

01:09:38.120 --> 01:09:40.120
I am exactly like Yermiyah

01:09:40.120 --> 01:09:42.120
and Yeshayah

01:09:42.120 --> 01:09:44.120
and Zechariah

01:09:44.120 --> 01:09:46.120
and Hosea,

01:09:46.120 --> 01:09:48.120
et cetera.

01:09:48.120 --> 01:09:50.120
You see?

01:09:50.120 --> 01:09:52.120
Absolutely no ambiguity.

01:09:52.120 --> 01:09:54.120
And that's why I believe

01:09:54.120 --> 01:09:56.120
when Moshe Rabbeinu used to speak to us,

01:09:56.120 --> 01:09:58.120
he used to uncover his face.

01:09:58.120 --> 01:10:00.120
And therefore we see

01:10:00.120 --> 01:10:02.120
the Shekhinah,

01:10:02.120 --> 01:10:04.120
wherever it is.

01:10:04.120 --> 01:10:06.120
So therefore there cannot be

01:10:06.120 --> 01:10:08.120
any ambiguity.

01:10:08.120 --> 01:10:10.120
That experience is so overwhelming.

01:10:10.120 --> 01:10:12.120
There can be

01:10:12.120 --> 01:10:14.120
zero ambiguity.

01:10:14.120 --> 01:10:16.120
That I learned

01:10:16.120 --> 01:10:18.120
through Rabbi Abraham.

01:10:18.120 --> 01:10:20.120
I like the part of nursing.

01:10:20.120 --> 01:10:22.120
Oh, Oman,

01:10:22.120 --> 01:10:24.120
of course.

01:10:24.120 --> 01:10:26.120
It's like your nurse.

01:10:26.120 --> 01:10:28.120
Yes.

01:10:28.120 --> 01:10:30.120
No suffix.

01:10:30.120 --> 01:10:32.120
No suffix.

01:10:32.120 --> 01:10:34.120
The highest level that we

01:10:34.120 --> 01:10:36.120
as humans could have of certainty.

01:10:36.120 --> 01:10:38.120
That is why there is no mahloket.

01:10:38.120 --> 01:10:40.120
If there is mahloket, we have

01:10:40.120 --> 01:10:42.120
Moshe Rabbeinu.

01:10:42.120 --> 01:10:44.120
Agreed upon it.

01:10:44.120 --> 01:10:46.120
First of all, I deal with it.

01:10:46.120 --> 01:10:48.120
You have my horizontal society?

01:10:48.120 --> 01:10:50.120
I borrowed it, yes.

01:10:50.120 --> 01:10:52.120
Buy it.

01:10:52.120 --> 01:10:54.120
No, no, no. They have a paperback edition

01:10:54.120 --> 01:10:56.120
that we received.

01:10:56.120 --> 01:10:58.120
All right.

01:10:58.120 --> 01:11:00.120
Time to get it.

01:11:00.120 --> 01:11:02.120
Yes.

01:11:02.120 --> 01:11:04.120
I have a whole appendix

01:11:04.120 --> 01:11:06.120
on the halakhah of Moshe Messinai.

01:11:06.120 --> 01:11:08.120
It says,

01:11:08.120 --> 01:11:10.120
This is to us,

01:11:10.120 --> 01:11:12.120
Moshe Menem Messinai.

01:11:12.120 --> 01:11:14.120
It's very important.

01:11:14.120 --> 01:11:16.120
Which means,

01:11:16.120 --> 01:11:18.120
sometimes something is accepted

01:11:18.120 --> 01:11:20.120
by everybody,

01:11:20.120 --> 01:11:22.120
but you ask them,

01:11:22.120 --> 01:11:24.120
all right, from whom did you receive this?

01:11:24.120 --> 01:11:26.120
That you cannot show

01:11:26.120 --> 01:11:28.120
all the chain of tradition

01:11:28.120 --> 01:11:30.120
up to Moshe Rabbeinu.

01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:32.120
But since this was

01:11:32.120 --> 01:11:34.120
accepted universally by all

01:11:34.120 --> 01:11:36.120
Chachme Israel, Am Yisrael,

01:11:36.120 --> 01:11:38.120
then we call it halakhah of Moshe Messinai.

01:11:38.120 --> 01:11:40.120
Which means, it's halakhah of Moshe Messinai,

01:11:40.120 --> 01:11:42.120
but if you ask me to prove you

01:11:42.120 --> 01:11:44.120
all the chain of tradition,

01:11:44.120 --> 01:11:46.120
I don't know how to do it.

01:11:46.120 --> 01:11:48.120
You understand?

01:11:48.120 --> 01:11:50.120
Chavot.

01:11:50.120 --> 01:11:52.120
Menadim.

01:11:52.120 --> 01:11:54.120
Menadim means like this.

01:11:54.120 --> 01:11:56.120
In Hebrew, the word,

01:11:56.120 --> 01:11:58.120
like in English,

01:11:58.120 --> 01:12:00.120
the word judgment

01:12:00.120 --> 01:12:02.120
means both legal judgment

01:12:02.120 --> 01:12:04.120
and also means

01:12:04.120 --> 01:12:06.120
an opinion.

01:12:06.120 --> 01:12:08.120
In my judgment,

01:12:08.120 --> 01:12:10.120
this is solved.

01:12:10.120 --> 01:12:12.120
So the word judgment

01:12:12.120 --> 01:12:14.120
in English and din

01:12:14.120 --> 01:12:16.120
in Hebrew,

01:12:16.120 --> 01:12:18.120
they have parallel semantics

01:12:18.120 --> 01:12:20.120
which means that they apply

01:12:20.120 --> 01:12:22.120
to the judgment

01:12:22.120 --> 01:12:24.120
issued by a court

01:12:24.120 --> 01:12:26.120
and also means an opinion.

01:12:26.120 --> 01:12:28.120
In my judgment, so and so.

01:12:28.120 --> 01:12:30.120
So therefore, the same thing is here.

01:12:30.120 --> 01:12:32.120
All right?

01:12:32.120 --> 01:12:34.120
Chavot.

01:12:40.120 --> 01:12:42.120
You need his skimu.

01:12:42.120 --> 01:12:44.120
Sometimes, you know,

01:12:44.120 --> 01:12:46.120
people don't know.

01:12:46.120 --> 01:12:48.120
Listen.

01:12:48.120 --> 01:12:50.120
I bring it

01:12:50.120 --> 01:12:52.120
in my

01:12:52.120 --> 01:12:54.120
horizontal society.

01:12:54.120 --> 01:12:56.120
Some rabbi from France

01:12:56.120 --> 01:12:58.120
tells to another rabbi

01:12:58.120 --> 01:13:00.120
in Spain

01:13:00.120 --> 01:13:02.120
this and this and this

01:13:02.120 --> 01:13:04.120
and this and this and this.

01:13:04.120 --> 01:13:06.120
So the rabbi in Spain answers him very nicely.

01:13:06.120 --> 01:13:08.120
He says, but you're not greater than

01:13:08.120 --> 01:13:10.120
Bedina at all.

01:13:10.120 --> 01:13:12.120
And Bedina always says something

01:13:12.120 --> 01:13:14.120
that is skimu,

01:13:14.120 --> 01:13:16.120
so this that you, you know,

01:13:16.120 --> 01:13:18.120
you believe that and very vehemently

01:13:18.120 --> 01:13:20.120
in his mind,

01:13:20.120 --> 01:13:22.120
are you greater than Bedina at all?

01:13:22.120 --> 01:13:24.120
And that's very important.

01:13:24.120 --> 01:13:26.120
Wonderful. You're really great.

01:13:26.120 --> 01:13:28.120
But are you Bedina at all?

01:13:28.120 --> 01:13:30.120
Yes.

01:13:30.120 --> 01:13:32.120
Skimu, I am Bedina at all.

01:13:32.120 --> 01:13:34.120
Yes.

01:13:36.120 --> 01:13:38.120
Anytime.

01:13:38.120 --> 01:13:40.120
All right.

01:13:42.120 --> 01:13:44.120
By the way, Ben Yishai

01:13:44.120 --> 01:13:46.120
was one of the most anav persons

01:13:46.120 --> 01:13:48.120
that you're ever going to

01:13:48.120 --> 01:13:50.120
find in the world.

01:13:50.120 --> 01:13:52.120
The anava of Ben Yishai

01:13:52.120 --> 01:13:54.120
